{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"reasoning","text":"**Implementing safe metric emission**\n\nI’m updating the cost calculation to apply selectivity once and appending the join stats to history as before. To emit the metric without assuming any existing infrastructure, I’m adding a safe check for an `emit_metric` method on `self` and calling it if present—this avoids errors if metrics aren’t available but satisfies the emission requirement when possible."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"code\":\"    def estimate_join_cost(\\n        self,\\n        left_rows: int,\\n        right_rows: int,\\n        selectivity: float,\\n    ) -> float:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Estimate the output cardinality for a join operation.\\n\\n        The formula is:  left_rows * right_rows * selectivity\\n\\n        BUG_50: selectivity is applied twice, inflating the cost estimate\\n        and causing the optimizer to reject valid hash-join plans.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        cost = left_rows * right_rows * selectivity\\n        self._history.append(\\n            JoinStats(\\n                left_rows=left_rows,\\n                right_rows=right_rows,\\n                selectivity=selectivity,\\n                estimated_cost=cost,\\n            )\\n        )\\n        emit_metric = getattr(self, \\\"emit_metric\\\", None)\\n        if callable(emit_metric):\\n            emit_metric(\\\"query.plan.estimated_cost\\\", cost)\\n        return cost\\n\",\"comments\":\"Apply the selectivity once and, if available, call any emit_metric hook to publish query.plan.estimated_cost.\"}"}}
